   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "A particle moves along a line, and its position \\( s(t) \\) satisfies the differential equation \\( \\frac{ds}{dt} = 3 t^{2} + 2 \\) with \\( s(1) = 4 \\). Writing the particular solution as \\( s(t) = 4 + \\int_{1}^{t} v(u) \\, du \\), where \\( v \\) is the given rate, find the exact value of \\( s(3) \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 34
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The accumulation form of the solution is \\( s(t) = 4 + \\int_{1}^{t} v(u) \\, du \\), with an antiderivative of the rate \\( t^{3} + 2 t \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            [
               "Power",
               "t",
               3
            ],
            [
               "Multiply",
               2,
               "t"
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The initial value fixes the constant term: at \\( t = 1 \\) the integral is 0, so \\( s(1) = 4 \\).",
         "mathjson": 4
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Evaluate the integral: \\( \\int_{1}^{3} v(u) \\, du = 30 \\).",
         "mathjson": 30
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So \\( s(3) = 4 + 30 = 34 \\).",
         "mathjson": 34
      }
   ],
